 qemu-server (9.2.24) trixie; urgency=medium
 
   * persist a generated MAC address for network devices without one when
     starting a VM, or when restoring a backup without 'unique'. Before, every
     user of the config got another random address, for example the VM, the
     SDN DHCP mapping and cloud-init. Starting such a VM thus changes its
     config once. A VM that resumes from a saved state or arrives through a
     live migration keeps running with the address it has, until its next
     cold start.
 
